/**
 * TackQuote admin Overview.
 *
 * One card per settings area in the WooCommerce plugin's tab order (Connection, Storefront,
 * B2B pricing, Buyer groups, Forms, Orders, Help), reached from the tab row at the top. Each
 * card shows what is switched on and links straight to its group in Stores > Configuration
 * (Block\Adminhtml\Dashboard::getGroupUrl()); the links are left out for an admin without
 * the configuration permission.
 *
 * CSP — the behaviour script goes out through SecureHtmlRenderer rather than as a literal
 * <script> tag, so Magento\Csp\Helper\InlineUtil can stamp it with the request nonce once a
 * merchant drops 'unsafe-inline' from script-src. Without that the "Test connection" button
 * is simply dead in the browser and nothing reaches var/log. $secureRenderer arrives as a
 * block variable from app/etc/di.xml; there is nothing to inject.
 *
 * The endpoint and the three status strings travel out of PHP as data attributes and
 * mage/translate lookups respectively, so the script itself is a constant with no
 * server-side interpolation to escape. The accent swatch is a hex colour validated by
 * Model\Styling\StyleRules and checked again here, applied through renderStyleAsTag() so no
 * inline style attribute is needed.
 *
 * @var \TackQuote\Quotes\Block\Adminhtml\Dashboard $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Helper\SecureHtmlRenderer $secureRenderer
 * @package TackQuote_Quotes
 */

